{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01210",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 8.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "Doctor, I've checked them in and done the the preliminary measurements, I'll hand them over when you ask."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.21,
      "end_seconds": 14.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.43,
      "end_seconds": 19.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.99,
      "end_seconds": 25.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 27.2,
      "end_seconds": 37.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.83,
      "text": "let me think, um, it's a dry cough that won't go away, doctor she didn't want to come, but I insisted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.29,
      "end_seconds": 40.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.57,
      "end_seconds": 46.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "I'm on valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 48.6,
      "end_seconds": 58.2,
      "duration_seconds": 9.6,
      "text": "doctor, um, I think the last prescription for the valsartan was 40 milligrams we changed it at the last visit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.16,
      "end_seconds": 64.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.71,
      "end_seconds": 71.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. Digene. I take it after meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.28,
      "end_seconds": 73.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.97,
      "end_seconds": 81.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "I'd say about a week actually, no, closer to to four weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.0,
      "end_seconds": 85.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.51,
      "end_seconds": 89.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "It's all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.31,
      "end_seconds": 94.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "So, does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.37,
      "end_seconds": 128.91,
      "duration_seconds": 33.54,
      "text": "A burning in the chest after meals goes along with it, uh, most of the time. The burning in the chest after meals? That's been for about three months. I've also had a sour taste in the mouth, for about a month. As for sour taste in the mouth, it's once or twice a day. There was a hoarse voice in the mornings, yes, but that went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.06,
      "end_seconds": 133.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "have you had shortness of breath, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.9,
      "end_seconds": 137.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "No. No shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.18,
      "end_seconds": 146.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.78,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any wheezing, night sweats, coughing up blood or trouble swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.05,
      "end_seconds": 155.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "I haven't had wheezing, night sweats, coughing up blood or trouble swallowing, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.64,
      "end_seconds": 159.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.51,
      "end_seconds": 163.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "no, you know, joints are fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.94,
      "end_seconds": 168.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.83,
      "end_seconds": 174.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "My father had bowel cancer. My cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.47,
      "end_seconds": 179.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.5,
      "end_seconds": 183.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.57,
      "end_seconds": 185.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.79,
      "end_seconds": 190.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.57,
      "end_seconds": 195.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.45,
      "end_seconds": 207.22,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "I mean, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago i don't remember which one, or what happened exactly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.34,
      "end_seconds": 226.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.34,
      "end_seconds": 229.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "no surgery, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.5,
      "end_seconds": 233.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.85,
      "end_seconds": 237.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 255.49,
      "end_seconds": 266.34,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Heart rate 83, SpO2 99 percent on room air, respiratory rate 18, blood pressure 110 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.06,
      "end_seconds": 267.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.51,
      "end_seconds": 273.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "let's move on to the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.79,
      "end_seconds": 287.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.71,
      "end_seconds": 292.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.13,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Chest is clear and the throat looks a little red at the back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.27,
      "end_seconds": 324.52,
      "duration_seconds": 13.25,
      "text": "Right, you can relax now. Right, here's what I'm thinking. I don't have a clear answer today: a cough driven by acid reflux is possible, and so is cough-variant asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.65,
      "end_seconds": 329.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.76,
      "end_seconds": 348.0,
      "duration_seconds": 17.24,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a cough driven by acid reflux. So, to recap quickly. You've had a dry cough that won't go away for four weeks, and no coughing up blood or wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.1,
      "end_seconds": 349.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.69,
      "end_seconds": 365.11,
      "duration_seconds": 14.42,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. For now, no new medicines or tests are needed. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.27,
      "end_seconds": 368.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "thank you, doctor, goodbye"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.04,
      "end_seconds": 371.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}